### 1. `selectProviderValue` — success when value is already correct

After the control is visible and enabled, **before** `provider.selectOption()` (which was stalling on native `<option>` visibility), the harness now:

- Reads `preSelectValue` from the `<select>`.
- If it already equals the target `value`, re-checks in the page that the matching **`<option>` exists and is not disabled** (presence + enabled, **not** visibility).
- If that passes, it **returns immediately** (no `selectOption`, no poll loop).
- For OpenRouter (`useOpenrouterArtifacts`), it logs and writes artifacts:

```997:1034:e2e/react-core.spec.js
        // Native <select> options are often present but not :visible while collapsed; Playwright selectOption
        // can wait on option visibility and stall even when the control value is already correct (25778492142).
        const preSelectValue = await provider
            .evaluate((el) => (el instanceof HTMLSelectElement ? String(el.value || '') : ''))
            .catch(() => '');
        if (preSelectValue === value) {
            const optReady = await page
                .evaluate((targetValue) => {
                    const el = document.querySelector(
                        '[data-testid="settings-connection-controls"] [data-testid="settings-provider-select"]',
                    );
                    if (!(el instanceof HTMLSelectElement)) return { ok: false, reason: 'not-select' };
                    const opt = Array.from(el.options).find((o) => String(o.value) === targetValue);
                    if (!opt) return { ok: false, reason: 'option-missing' };
                    return { ok: true, optionDisabled: Boolean(opt.disabled) };
                }, value)
                .catch(() => ({ ok: false, reason: 'evaluate-error' }));
            if (optReady && optReady.ok === true && !optReady.optionDisabled) {
                if (useOpenrouterArtifacts && value === 'openrouter') {
                    console.log('offline-kill-provider-select-openrouter-already-selected=true');
                    console.log('offline-kill-provider-select-openrouter-success-by-value=true');
                    await writeOpenrouterArtifact('after-select-attempt.json', {
                        classification: 'provider-select-skipped-already-value',
                        phase: 'after-select-attempt',
                        skippedSelect: true,
                        preSelectValue,
                        ...(await providerSelectMinimalContext(page)),
                    });
                    await writeOpenrouterArtifact('after-success.json', {
                        classification: 'provider-select-after-success',
                        phase: 'after-success',
                        skippedSelect: true,
                        preSelectValue,
                        ...(await providerSelectMinimalContext(page)),
                    });
                }
                return provider;
            }
        }
```

So the same case as run **25778492142** (`current-value=openrouter`, option present, option not “visible”) should **short-circuit** instead of burning the stage on `selectOption`.

### 2. Timeout classifier — `unknown-timeout` vs real buckets

```1675:1689:e2e/react-core.spec.js
        if (!st.openrouterOptionPresent) {
            return 'offline-kill-provider-select-openrouter-option-missing';
