content.text:
Here is what was implemented to finish the OpenRouter provider-select harness work.

### Behavior

1. **`lastOpenrouterSelectHarnessDiag`** – Cleared at the start of each OpenRouter `selectProviderValue` run, then filled across:
   - pre–`selectOption` probe (`captureOpenrouterProviderSelectHarness`)
   - native-fallback entry (fresh `readVal` + probe)
   - extended **`page.evaluate`** for native set (value before/after set, after `input`/`change`, indices, option values, OpenRouter option flags, `openrouterSelectReactResetAfterFallback`)
   - post–read-after-select probe (stable `before->after`, counts, remount hint)
   - poll failure (`finalizeOpenrouterPollFailureHarness`) before any poll-phase `throwOpenrouterFailed`

2. **`throwOpenrouterFailed`** – Merges the harness object into the failed artifact payload (before `extra`, so callers can still override).

3. **`emitProviderSelectOpenrouterTimeoutDiagnostics`** – Merges `...harness` into the timeout JSON, refines **`offline-kill-provider-select-openrouter-classification`** when inner classification is a **poll** failure via `classifyProviderSelectOpenrouterPollHarness`, logs `offline-kill-provider-select-openrouter-harness-*` lines for all `openrouter*` / `providerSelect*` harness keys, and logs `harness-refined-classification` / inner-PC when refinement changes the bucket.

4. **Poll throws** – `helperTimeoutStage: 'poll'` is attached for the three poll failure paths so refinement stays aligned with stage metadata.

5. **`governance/source_manifest.json`** – Updated by `node scripts/update-source-manifest-hashes.js` (required after touching `e2e/react-core.spec.js`).

### Key code references

```909:946:c:\Users\KickA\Documents\GitHub\NeuralShell\e2e\react-core.spec.js
    function classifyProviderSelectOpenrouterPollHarness(innerPc, helperStage, harness, orState) {
        const h = harness && typeof harness === 'object' ? harness : {};
        const pc = String(innerPc || '').trim();
        const hs = String(helperStage || '').trim();
        const pollish = pc === 'provider-select-poll-timeout' || (pc === 'provider-select-helper-timeout' && hs === 'poll');
        if (!pollish) return null;
        if (h.providerSelectRemountedDuringFallback === true) {
            return 'provider-select-control-remounted-during-fallback';
        }
        // ... option / react / empty-value buckets ...
        return 'provider-select-poll-timeout-value-empty';
    }
```

```819:907:c:\Users\KickA\Documents\GitHub\NeuralShell\e2e\react-core.spec.js
    async function captureOpenrouterProviderSelectHarness(pg, providerLoc) {
        // providerSelectCount, scoped query snapshot, locator vs querySelector identity,
        // openrouterSelectTagName / IsNativeSelect / Connected / Disabled / options / openrouter option flags
    }
```

Refinement and harness merge in **`emitProviderSelectOpenrouterTimeoutDiagnostics`** (around lines 3810–3890 in your tree) drive the next CI line: **`offline-kill-provider-select-openrouter-classification=`** should now resolve to one of the requested **`provider-select-*`** strings whenever the inner error is **`provider-select-poll-timeout`** (with harness data present).

ESLint on `e2e/react-core.spec.js` passes. If you want this as a commit, say so and we can stage `e2e/react-core.spec.js` and `governance/source_manifest.json` only.

